1
00:00:15,011 --> 00:00:24,791
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,609 --> 00:02:08,609
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:12,184 --> 00:02:12,994
Father.

4
00:02:14,287 --> 00:02:15,577
You may speak my daughter.

5
00:02:21,083 --> 00:02:22,233
What’s wrong?

6
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:26,180
You seem like as if something is
bothering you.

7
00:02:34,391 --> 00:02:35,441
Sing your heart out.

8
00:02:40,392 --> 00:02:43,022
There is something you need to
know, father.

9
00:02:57,873 --> 00:02:58,613
Father.

10
00:03:00,617 --> 00:03:01,547
Dündar Bey!

11
00:03:10,954 --> 00:03:11,924
Aygül Hatun.

12
00:03:12,836 --> 00:03:14,356
There are important issues.

13
00:03:15,268 --> 00:03:16,418
Excuse us.

14
00:03:36,491 --> 00:03:38,301
What’s the matter, Alişar Bey?

15
00:03:38,494 --> 00:03:42,014
Gündüz Bey and Dahi Bey are coming here.

16
00:03:42,297 --> 00:03:46,377
As a Bannerlord, I'd like to
regulate things once again.

17
00:03:47,030 --> 00:03:49,240
You demand what is rightfully yours.

18
00:03:51,277 --> 00:03:52,537
I say...

19
00:03:53,778 --> 00:03:55,698
...that we capture Gündüz now.

20
00:03:56,705 --> 00:03:59,445
From here to Tent, go as the true Bey.

21
00:04:01,053 --> 00:04:03,643
And settle down Kayı Tent once again.

22
00:04:04,673 --> 00:04:05,493
Why not?

23
00:04:07,631 --> 00:04:08,351
But…

24
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:12,220
...what are we going to about Osman?
Alişar Bey?

25
00:04:14,582 --> 00:04:16,302
And also, what about Balgay?

26
00:04:17,485 --> 00:04:20,535
If I settle down the Bey Tent...

27
00:04:21,871 --> 00:04:25,251
...it's obvious how will Osman answer
to that.

28
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,787
Balgay is already hostile to us.

29
00:04:29,924 --> 00:04:32,344
He can form an alliance with Osman.

30
00:04:33,252 --> 00:04:37,252
We might have to fight with both of them.

31
00:04:38,061 --> 00:04:40,461
If Osman and Balgay made an alliance...

32
00:04:42,237 --> 00:04:44,307
...it means the apocalypse is already
here.

33
00:04:45,788 --> 00:04:48,238
Don’t you dare to think it’s impossible
Alişar Bey.

34
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:56,630
I have seen so many incidents like
this in my life.

35
00:04:59,458 --> 00:05:02,938
Then we will take them down together.

36
00:05:04,335 --> 00:05:05,725
Geyhatu supports us.

37
00:05:06,365 --> 00:05:10,365
He asks for Osman and Genghis' Laws
from us.

38
00:05:10,923 --> 00:05:14,653
You just continue to stand as hard as
a rock.

39
00:05:16,686 --> 00:05:17,426
Then..

40
00:05:18,932 --> 00:05:22,072
...Gündüz will end up in a cage when he
arrives.

41
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:27,380
If needed, he may be free to give his
life.

42
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:33,130
He will understand what trying to replace
me stands for.

43
00:05:33,905 --> 00:05:34,935
After him...

44
00:05:35,610 --> 00:05:38,230
...we will decide what to do about
Osman and Balgay.

45
00:05:39,409 --> 00:05:40,339
Alişar Bey!

46
00:05:41,129 --> 00:05:44,989
My heart is lit with the fire of revenge.

47
00:05:45,546 --> 00:05:50,816
May breathing be illicit to me before
I wreak their spite.

48
00:05:54,488 --> 00:05:55,378
Illicit.

49
00:06:02,415 --> 00:06:04,175
Where are the Laws, Osman?

50
00:06:04,615 --> 00:06:06,325
So that we came to terms…

51
00:06:06,978 --> 00:06:10,388
…and you agreed to die with me…

52
00:06:11,865 --> 00:06:13,605
…you need to tell me where they are.

53
00:06:15,199 --> 00:06:16,759
Why are these laws...

54
00:06:18,487 --> 00:06:20,437
...very important for you?

55
00:06:20,571 --> 00:06:24,171
When it comes to Genghis Khan…

56
00:06:26,644 --> 00:06:29,264
…we can burn the whole world down, Osman.

57
00:06:30,367 --> 00:06:33,687
Before him we were nothing but
pathetic people…

58
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:36,067
…then he made us become superior to
everybody.

59
00:06:36,904 --> 00:06:39,464
We did not have a country before
he came into power.

60
00:06:39,464 --> 00:06:41,624
Now all the world is ours.

61
00:06:42,886 --> 00:06:44,826
You make a God out of Genghis.

62
00:06:48,235 --> 00:06:51,755
The only thing you worship is fighting…

63
00:06:52,259 --> 00:06:53,239
…and pillaging.

64
00:06:56,821 --> 00:06:59,131
For now, maybe you are victorious.

65
00:06:59,429 --> 00:07:00,579
However…

66
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:03,988
…you lack the soul to clench victory.

67
00:07:05,502 --> 00:07:08,362
Souls are always with us.

68
00:07:09,857 --> 00:07:12,257
Every single shaman give power to us.

69
00:07:13,179 --> 00:07:15,199
What are you talking about?

70
00:07:16,517 --> 00:07:18,627
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

71
00:07:22,324 --> 00:07:24,074
''O Unbelievers...''

72
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:29,870
''…if you prayed for victory. Now has
the victory come to you..''

73
00:07:32,634 --> 00:07:35,694
''If you desist from wrong…''

74
00:07:36,365 --> 00:07:38,005
''…it will be the best for you.''

75
00:07:38,457 --> 00:07:41,217
''If you return…''

76
00:07:42,227 --> 00:07:43,607
''…so shall we.''

77
00:07:45,836 --> 00:07:51,276
''Not the least good will your forces be
to you even if they were multiplied.

78
00:07:56,404 --> 00:08:01,424
''Allah is with those who believe.''

79
00:08:05,672 --> 00:08:08,272
You people do not understand.

80
00:08:08,859 --> 00:08:10,689
Your land is ours now…

81
00:08:11,839 --> 00:08:13,419
…as well as your palaces.

82
00:08:13,861 --> 00:08:16,761
And those sons and daughters of you
have started to serve us.

83
00:08:16,761 --> 00:08:18,421
You pay taxes every year.

84
00:08:18,496 --> 00:08:20,206
Where is your God now?

85
00:08:20,206 --> 00:08:21,316
Where is he?

86
00:08:22,768 --> 00:08:25,188
Don’t let the time Allah spared for
tyrants...

87
00:08:25,615 --> 00:08:27,265
...spoil you, Balgay.

88
00:08:30,079 --> 00:08:33,569
The words that Pharaoh and Nimrod once
spoke are very similar to yours.

89
00:08:34,850 --> 00:08:38,310
When Allah finally decides to punish you…

90
00:08:39,511 --> 00:08:41,481
…you will not be guarded...

91
00:08:41,779 --> 00:08:43,809
...neither by your soldiers...

92
00:08:45,334 --> 00:08:47,264
...nor your Noyans.

93
00:08:52,243 --> 00:08:53,563
Enough non sense!

94
00:08:55,893 --> 00:08:57,493
Where are the Laws?

95
00:08:59,094 --> 00:09:02,004
First, I need to be sure that you
are telling the truth.

96
00:09:03,304 --> 00:09:05,744
Is my uncle with Alişar right now?

97
00:09:06,699 --> 00:09:09,979
My birds told me so.

98
00:09:10,791 --> 00:09:11,911
So far…

99
00:09:13,004 --> 00:09:14,904
…they have never been wrong.

100
00:09:16,016 --> 00:09:17,676
We will see.

101
00:09:32,973 --> 00:09:34,463
Do you have water?

102
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,900
I will take ablution and do my prayers.

103
00:09:43,290 --> 00:09:45,050
Then, we will be on our way.

104
00:09:45,050 --> 00:09:46,800
It is not the time for your prayers.

105
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:47,980
Our enemies are waiting.

106
00:09:49,883 --> 00:09:52,883
For us, nothing comes before praying.

107
00:09:56,333 --> 00:09:57,403
You shall wait.

108
00:10:10,869 --> 00:10:12,039
Put it there.

109
00:10:46,638 --> 00:10:48,168
What is he doing?

110
00:10:49,213 --> 00:10:51,583
He cleansed himself to worship.

111
00:10:59,323 --> 00:11:01,983
How can you trust him, Commander Balgay?

112
00:11:02,573 --> 00:11:04,363
Who said I trust him?

113
00:11:08,481 --> 00:11:13,551
He betrayed me and sought to save his
Tent at the first opportunity.

114
00:11:15,524 --> 00:11:17,144
We will wait for a while.

115
00:11:18,147 --> 00:11:19,137
Be cautious.

116
00:11:19,713 --> 00:11:22,203
Keep your ears and eyes wide open.

117
00:11:46,106 --> 00:11:48,616
All preperations are over, Gündüz Bey.

118
00:11:48,616 --> 00:11:50,306
We are ready for your commands.

119
00:11:50,306 --> 00:11:52,896
I want everybody to be cautious, Ayaz.

120
00:11:53,226 --> 00:11:55,446
We can’t predict what that Alişar Dog
will do.

121
00:12:01,517 --> 00:12:02,567
Alps!

122
00:12:03,101 --> 00:12:06,361
If we end up in an ambush...

123
00:12:06,361 --> 00:12:09,351
...we will send all of them to hell!

124
00:12:09,351 --> 00:12:11,131
As you command, my Bey!

125
00:12:12,093 --> 00:12:13,383
How magnificent!

126
00:12:14,154 --> 00:12:15,614
How magnificent!

127
00:12:16,219 --> 00:12:18,389
How magnificent my Valiants are.

128
00:12:18,796 --> 00:12:21,896
Praise be!

129
00:12:22,838 --> 00:12:24,048
How magnificent!

130
00:12:36,444 --> 00:12:39,054
I see an army of steel.

131
00:12:40,237 --> 00:12:44,597
As expected from my Gündüz Bey.

132
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:49,710
You once said reputation is more
important than swords, Bamsı Bey.

133
00:12:50,284 --> 00:12:52,444
To bring the enemy to his knees...

134
00:12:52,804 --> 00:12:55,748
...eventually one must use the power of
fear, you said.

135
00:12:58,328 --> 00:13:00,678
We are trying our best...

136
00:13:01,542 --> 00:13:03,572
...to follow and execute your words.

137
00:13:04,010 --> 00:13:06,380
Praise be upon you, my Gündüz.

138
00:13:07,675 --> 00:13:11,845
My Gündüz, I will be waiting for your
orders at the Tent.

139
00:13:12,107 --> 00:13:15,217
For certain, Alişar will try to play
games on us.

140
00:13:15,594 --> 00:13:20,194
In case of anything, I will organize the
rest for rioting against them.

141
00:13:20,194 --> 00:13:22,974
We will create an army of children if
necessary.

142
00:13:23,541 --> 00:13:25,631
After all, we are all born soldiers.

143
00:13:25,631 --> 00:13:26,881
An army as a nation.

144
00:13:28,683 --> 00:13:32,883
May Allah forbid Alişar and my uncle
make such mistakes.

145
00:13:33,663 --> 00:13:35,323
With the name of Allah.

146
00:13:36,587 --> 00:13:38,577
Are there any news from Osman, Bamsı Bey?

147
00:13:38,826 --> 00:13:42,066
That I’m also hesitant about, my Gündüz.

148
00:13:42,096 --> 00:13:43,366
It’s been too long.

149
00:13:59,388 --> 00:14:00,368
Burhan?

150
00:14:05,363 --> 00:14:07,463
Where is my Osman, Burhan?

151
00:14:32,027 --> 00:14:33,267
Look at him!

152
00:14:34,522 --> 00:14:36,842
We can cut his throat if we want to.

153
00:14:37,662 --> 00:14:39,462
As if he is afraid of nothing.

154
00:14:43,111 --> 00:14:47,291
Dying for his faith is what a Muslim
wants the most.

155
00:14:52,027 --> 00:14:53,927
His faith is harder than a rock.

156
00:14:54,791 --> 00:14:57,041
If we had even a bit of his faith…

157
00:14:57,854 --> 00:15:00,504
…the whole world would be worshipping to
us by now.

158
00:15:22,115 --> 00:15:22,935
My Allah.

159
00:15:24,053 --> 00:15:26,443
Protect me from heathens.

160
00:15:28,146 --> 00:15:30,296
There is no true deity except you.

161
00:15:32,341 --> 00:15:35,411
You are the only one who has greatness.

162
00:15:37,471 --> 00:15:42,401
You are the only ruler of seven skies and
the almighty throne.

163
00:15:44,037 --> 00:15:48,647
I exonerate you from every physical
attributives.

164
00:15:49,938 --> 00:15:52,768
Being thankful is only reserved to you.

165
00:15:53,277 --> 00:15:56,697
You my Allah who rule all the realms.

166
00:15:59,896 --> 00:16:00,866
My Allah...

167
00:16:02,705 --> 00:16:04,635
...let my sword be sharp.

168
00:16:06,121 --> 00:16:07,911
And protect my path.

169
00:16:09,889 --> 00:16:13,339
Let us be victorious against all
tyrants, my Allah.

170
00:16:22,017 --> 00:16:23,117
-Father!
-Husband?

171
00:16:23,117 --> 00:16:24,177
Konur!

172
00:16:24,177 --> 00:16:24,997
Göktuğ!

173
00:16:26,843 --> 00:16:28,033
-Husband!?
-Father!?

174
00:17:03,918 --> 00:17:05,298
Let’s be on our way already!

175
00:17:05,298 --> 00:17:06,938
We lost time because of you.

176
00:17:07,823 --> 00:17:08,763
Balgay!

177
00:17:10,790 --> 00:17:12,720
Why are you in such hurry?

178
00:17:14,335 --> 00:17:16,715
Walking on the same path with me has
a price.

179
00:17:18,467 --> 00:17:20,257
You are already scared.

180
00:17:22,967 --> 00:17:23,997
Wait.

181
00:17:46,844 --> 00:17:48,584
We better go separately...

182
00:17:49,549 --> 00:17:51,359
...as to hide our alliance.

183
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:00,400
Let’s go.

184
00:18:27,025 --> 00:18:27,815
Go!

185
00:18:50,336 --> 00:18:52,166
What are you up to, Boran?

186
00:18:53,806 --> 00:18:56,726
What do you mean you left Osman alone
with Balgay’s soldiers?

187
00:19:00,961 --> 00:19:01,661
Tell me!

188
00:19:04,272 --> 00:19:05,622
What kind of an Alp are you?

189
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,980
How can you do this, Boran?

190
00:19:13,950 --> 00:19:15,840
Osman Bey ordered me to do so.

191
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,150
We can’t question.

192
00:19:19,947 --> 00:19:22,347
He ordered me to leave.

193
00:19:23,065 --> 00:19:24,485
And now I am here.

194
00:19:27,018 --> 00:19:29,658
Perhaps, my Bey already knows what is
best for him.

195
00:19:39,917 --> 00:19:40,617
Alps!

196
00:19:41,999 --> 00:19:43,789
We are not going to Alişar’s mansion.

197
00:19:43,789 --> 00:19:46,389
Instead, we will search every corner
of the whole forest.

198
00:19:47,387 --> 00:19:49,537
Don’t come back before you find my
brother.

199
00:19:49,537 --> 00:19:50,857
As you command, my Bey!

200
00:19:50,857 --> 00:19:52,487
Go now!

201
00:20:11,551 --> 00:20:12,301
Gündüz Bey.

202
00:20:12,301 --> 00:20:13,211
What?!

203
00:20:15,174 --> 00:20:16,894
Our guest is very important.

204
00:20:19,821 --> 00:20:22,511
Princess Adelfa, nephew of the
Byzantine Emperor.

205
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,890
Nephew of the emperor, huh?

206
00:20:41,278 --> 00:20:42,178
Tell me more.

207
00:20:43,495 --> 00:20:45,055
If Osman Bey didn’t forbid...

208
00:20:45,055 --> 00:20:47,495
... she would have been married to
Geyhatu by now.

209
00:20:52,849 --> 00:20:54,419
If the marriage happened...

210
00:20:55,101 --> 00:20:58,351
... It would have been
many Oghuzs' nightmare.

211
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:03,260
This is the reason why Osman ordered
you to leave with the Princess...

212
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:04,850
...at the cost of his own life.

213
00:21:13,495 --> 00:21:14,675
My Bey.

214
00:21:14,849 --> 00:21:17,059
He ordered me to entrust the Princess
to you.

215
00:21:17,603 --> 00:21:20,843
Keep her as a secret and don’t relieve
her identity.

216
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:24,040
My Allah protect Osman please.

217
00:21:35,622 --> 00:21:37,822
Welcome to the Kayı Tent, Princess.

218
00:21:42,222 --> 00:21:43,442
Aunt Selcan...

219
00:21:44,665 --> 00:21:46,375
...take care of our guest.

220
00:21:47,147 --> 00:21:50,217
But let nobody know about her existence.

221
00:21:54,755 --> 00:21:55,985
I appreciate it.

222
00:21:59,431 --> 00:21:59,506
I hope I will not disturb you.

223
00:21:59,506 --> 00:22:01,251
I hope I will not disturb you.
I hope I will not disturb you.

224
00:22:01,251 --> 00:22:01,376
I hope I will not disturb you.

225
00:22:01,773 --> 00:22:04,043
You are our guest, my daughter.

226
00:22:04,043 --> 00:22:06,122
You have place above our head.

227
00:22:09,956 --> 00:22:10,836
Bala.

228
00:22:11,372 --> 00:22:12,652
Come with us.

229
00:22:15,771 --> 00:22:16,991
Follow me, my daughter.

230
00:22:34,704 --> 00:22:36,424
Ohhh!

231
00:22:39,076 --> 00:22:41,246
Ohh, Osman!

232
00:22:42,078 --> 00:22:46,238
How could you risk your life like this?

233
00:22:49,642 --> 00:22:50,822
Gündüz Bey.

234
00:22:52,726 --> 00:22:55,806
If you allow me, I’d like to help
the other Alps with tracking.

235
00:23:14,470 --> 00:23:18,470
There is a secret behind this, my Gündüz.

236
00:23:19,184 --> 00:23:21,074
Something fishy, indeed.

237
00:23:22,841 --> 00:23:24,501
What do you mean, Bamsı Bey?

238
00:23:24,501 --> 00:23:25,851
My Gündüz.

239
00:23:26,649 --> 00:23:32,219
Osman saved the girl
while Balgay was there.

240
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:36,270
So it means there will be no war.

241
00:23:37,845 --> 00:23:39,655
But peace, my Gündüz.

242
00:23:41,465 --> 00:23:45,465
Balgay will try to form an
alliance with my Osman.

243
00:24:16,314 --> 00:24:19,574
Make your mind one with love, son.

244
00:24:19,975 --> 00:24:26,325
So that these dark clouds over
the world of Islam scatter.

245
00:24:26,698 --> 00:24:31,558
So that hopelessness comes to an end,
laziness comes to an end.

246
00:24:32,342 --> 00:24:36,342
So the fire of ressurection is rekindled.

247
00:24:36,658 --> 00:24:38,468
Eventually, my Sheikh.

248
00:24:41,889 --> 00:24:48,069
Allow me to always use my mind and
heart for you, my Allah.

249
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:07,150
You will never stop, will you?

250
00:25:07,784 --> 00:25:13,464
I won't, mother. You're not ashamed of
what you've done, but I am.

251
00:25:14,361 --> 00:25:17,851
My father will eventually find out.
It's better if he hears it from me.

252
00:25:21,289 --> 00:25:24,689
If you tell him and if he finds
out about Dündar Bey...

253
00:25:24,689 --> 00:25:26,889
... you very well know what
will happen to me.

254
00:25:29,971 --> 00:25:32,141
You're not thinking well, Aygül.

255
00:25:33,202 --> 00:25:35,112
Tomorrow is uncertain.

256
00:25:38,233 --> 00:25:42,823
Are you thinking well, mother?
It shows.

257
00:25:46,676 --> 00:25:49,636
You always compared
my brother Batur to Osman.

258
00:25:50,618 --> 00:25:54,618
You always blamed Osman
to make my brother shine out.

259
00:25:54,968 --> 00:25:58,797
You pushed and pushed my father.
Then it wasn't enough and--

260
00:25:58,797 --> 00:25:59,907
It wasn't enough.

261
00:26:00,792 --> 00:26:03,782
It wasn't enough. You're right.

262
00:26:06,513 --> 00:26:13,663
Your father couldn't handle it.
And as a mother, I did what was necessary.

263
00:26:14,986 --> 00:26:19,196
Look. With the Mongol's orders...

264
00:26:19,910 --> 00:26:22,720
... your father is talking to
the Banner Lord Alişar Bey...

265
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:25,000
... about how to hunt Osman down.

266
00:26:25,732 --> 00:26:27,202
Are we any different?

267
00:26:29,913 --> 00:26:31,923
My father is a Bey!

268
00:26:32,265 --> 00:26:34,635
While he has to take care of
the whole tent...

269
00:26:34,635 --> 00:26:37,359
... while there is chaos in the borders...

270
00:26:37,359 --> 00:26:40,789
... it is his duty to
do what politics require.

271
00:26:41,297 --> 00:26:45,297
What about you? Was it your duty?

272
00:26:47,978 --> 00:26:51,978
My father is loyal to his tent
and his traditions.

273
00:26:52,874 --> 00:26:55,284
You betrayed, mother.

274
00:26:58,052 --> 00:27:02,052
The difference is your treachery.

275
00:27:03,773 --> 00:27:08,473
If you think that way, my child, so be it.

276
00:27:09,163 --> 00:27:13,163
A mother does everything to
protect her children.

277
00:27:15,385 --> 00:27:20,805
But what can that mother do
if her child calls her a traitor?

278
00:27:24,645 --> 00:27:27,545
I don't care about anything
outside my family.

279
00:27:28,685 --> 00:27:31,565
I want you to be well.

280
00:27:34,457 --> 00:27:40,377
Know this. If someone was to
hurt a single hair of yours...

281
00:27:41,044 --> 00:27:45,044
... and if only the Mongols could
help me, I would ask them for help.

282
00:27:46,379 --> 00:27:51,869
Instead of throwing you into the fire,
I'd rather burn myself.

283
00:27:57,099 --> 00:27:59,209
I will stay quiet on one condition,
mother.

284
00:28:03,066 --> 00:28:05,576
Tell my father yourself.

285
00:28:08,897 --> 00:28:13,997
If he learns it from some one else,
it will be much worse for you.

286
00:28:44,391 --> 00:28:45,631
Helen!

287
00:28:47,958 --> 00:28:51,798
Where is Princess Sofia?
They said she wasn't in the castle.

288
00:28:51,798 --> 00:28:53,708
He went to an important meeting.

289
00:28:53,879 --> 00:28:56,629
As the castle's Commander,
why am I not aware of this?

290
00:28:58,247 --> 00:29:03,417
Even though you promised, you couldn't
find out where Osman is, Salvador.

291
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:06,840
You better think about this first.

292
00:29:08,386 --> 00:29:12,386
I know every place they go,
every whole they get into.

293
00:29:13,127 --> 00:29:15,977
Our soldiers are tracking him everywhere.

294
00:29:16,312 --> 00:29:17,802
Eventually--

295
00:29:19,604 --> 00:29:22,374
Eventually, you'll find him. I'm sure.

296
00:29:23,224 --> 00:29:25,244
Princess Sofia knows this as well.

297
00:29:31,849 --> 00:29:33,109
Helen.

298
00:29:46,821 --> 00:29:49,441
Alişar Bey must learn about these facts
as well.

299
00:29:50,653 --> 00:29:51,953
Okay.

300
00:29:54,810 --> 00:29:58,030
That's Master Yannis' spy.

301
00:29:59,269 --> 00:30:02,469
If he's here, there
must be important developments.

302
00:30:03,695 --> 00:30:04,865
Osman.

303
00:30:05,822 --> 00:30:07,092
He's back.

304
00:30:07,949 --> 00:30:09,829
With Balgay.

305
00:30:10,985 --> 00:30:14,395
They united against Princess Sofia.

306
00:30:14,731 --> 00:30:17,391
That's impossible.
Osman will never--

307
00:30:17,876 --> 00:30:20,456
Salvador...
Salvador...

308
00:30:20,635 --> 00:30:22,615
You still don't now who Osman is.

309
00:30:22,959 --> 00:30:25,459
And you say that you'll find him.

310
00:30:39,669 --> 00:30:43,669
I hope Osman doesn't get in trouble
because of a Byzantinian lady.

311
00:30:46,220 --> 00:30:50,730
Bala? My daughter, are you jealous?

312
00:30:52,277 --> 00:30:56,277
No, Selcan mother.
I'm worried about Osman.

313
00:30:56,407 --> 00:31:00,407
While we're on the topic, here's a
couple of advice from mother Selcan.

314
00:31:00,407 --> 00:31:02,547
They shall be a lesson to you.

315
00:31:03,427 --> 00:31:05,747
My Osman is a known Valiant.

316
00:31:05,747 --> 00:31:10,127
A mad valiant.
A handsome one at that.

317
00:31:12,764 --> 00:31:16,764
There will be lots of women
who want to be his wife.

318
00:31:17,242 --> 00:31:20,292
You need to prepare for that.

319
00:31:31,546 --> 00:31:33,206
Praise be!

320
00:31:33,771 --> 00:31:35,551
Does it look good?

321
00:31:36,127 --> 00:31:38,617
You're outstanding, my Princess daughter.

322
00:31:45,785 --> 00:31:47,755
We should settle you down here.

323
00:31:53,385 --> 00:31:56,565
We have lots of Valiant Alps
next to Osman Bey.

324
00:31:56,565 --> 00:31:58,615
We'll espouse you with one of them.

325
00:31:58,615 --> 00:32:01,157
They can't give you palaces like Geyhatu.

326
00:32:01,157 --> 00:32:04,017
But they will make their
home a palace for you.

327
00:32:04,017 --> 00:32:08,137
I'd rather go to hell than go
through that other marriage.

328
00:32:09,131 --> 00:32:11,391
This place is heaven next
to that, believe me.

329
00:32:14,651 --> 00:32:16,031
Come on.

330
00:32:31,085 --> 00:32:33,785
Tell me. How did these things happen?

331
00:32:33,907 --> 00:32:37,217
Messengers have been coming to
Constantinople for months.

332
00:32:37,545 --> 00:32:41,995
Geyhatu finally convinced the Emperor to
marry him through letters and gifts.

333
00:32:44,382 --> 00:32:46,042
I didn't want to.

334
00:32:46,879 --> 00:32:50,879
I prayed a lot. I begged that
this marriage didn't happen.

335
00:32:51,782 --> 00:32:54,872
Thankfully, Jesus almighty heard my voice.

336
00:32:55,696 --> 00:32:57,566
He sent Osman Bey.

337
00:32:59,928 --> 00:33:03,928
Geyhatu's plans were
hindered by Osman, thankfully.

338
00:33:05,787 --> 00:33:11,617
Who knows what other troubles
these Mongols would have caused us.

339
00:33:29,123 --> 00:33:31,693
Osman Bey is a real hero

340
00:33:32,362 --> 00:33:34,652
He saved me from those tyrants.

341
00:33:35,950 --> 00:33:38,140
You should have seen that moment!

342
00:33:38,531 --> 00:33:40,591
He risked his life for me.

343
00:33:41,828 --> 00:33:43,448
A real hero.

344
00:33:48,038 --> 00:33:50,098
May Jesus Christ protect him.

345
00:33:50,656 --> 00:33:55,116
Mother Mary forbid if something happens
to Osman Bey, I can't forgive myself.

346
00:33:56,126 --> 00:33:57,586
My daughter!

347
00:34:00,283 --> 00:34:04,283
I have to take care of something.
Take care of the Princess.

348
00:34:10,304 --> 00:34:12,964
Don't you worry, Selcan mother.

349
00:34:17,596 --> 00:34:18,796
Okay then.

350
00:34:34,110 --> 00:34:38,450
It seems that what Balgay has done
troubled Geyhatu.

351
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:41,851
He wants to regulate the lands.

352
00:34:41,851 --> 00:34:45,401
He wants to do it with you.

353
00:34:46,149 --> 00:34:48,749
The fact that he shared
his plans with you...

354
00:34:48,749 --> 00:34:53,369
... shows that you're still
in charge, Alişar Bey.

355
00:34:56,270 --> 00:35:00,270
I am no more, Dündar Bey.
It's us from now on.

356
00:35:00,881 --> 00:35:02,951
We're already connected by spirit.

357
00:35:03,594 --> 00:35:08,644
No one can destroy our alliance
once we're connected by blood as well.

358
00:35:09,728 --> 00:35:13,448
We'll start with Kayı Tent.

359
00:35:15,056 --> 00:35:17,216
Once we take your throne back.

360
00:35:17,216 --> 00:35:19,716
We won't go far with just words,
Alişar Bey.

361
00:35:21,060 --> 00:35:23,370
A bloody fight awaits us.

362
00:35:24,536 --> 00:35:29,046
I can't rest before I take
my son's revenge!

363
00:35:30,624 --> 00:35:34,224
I can't sleep.
I have to take my Batur's revenge.

364
00:35:37,190 --> 00:35:42,080
Once you take the throne back and become
both the Kayı's bey and the land's Bey...

365
00:35:43,248 --> 00:35:45,018
... the rest is easy.

366
00:35:45,803 --> 00:35:51,863
Those who killed my son-in-law
will regret what they have done.

367
00:35:53,363 --> 00:35:57,553
There will be people who don't
want me to get back on the throne.

368
00:35:58,529 --> 00:36:01,919
There will be lots of noise.

369
00:36:02,785 --> 00:36:04,575
Why do we feed all these soldiers?

370
00:36:05,854 --> 00:36:08,914
Why do we host Geyhatu's soldiers?

371
00:36:11,110 --> 00:36:16,220
If they can't do their jobs
when the time comes...

372
00:36:16,911 --> 00:36:20,771
... why do we keep all these
dogs tied up in here?

373
00:36:21,786 --> 00:36:24,456
We'll besiege the Tent.

374
00:36:25,503 --> 00:36:28,413
Then we'll get them!

375
00:36:29,871 --> 00:36:33,871
Those who are connected to you will not
be just watching I suppose.

376
00:36:34,499 --> 00:36:38,149
We'll drown them in the blood
they spilt, Dündar Bey!

377
00:36:58,462 --> 00:37:01,662
The Mongols won't let go
of this, Bala Hatun.

378
00:37:02,692 --> 00:37:04,522
You're in danger because of me.

379
00:37:05,883 --> 00:37:08,083
Not because of you, Princess.

380
00:37:08,525 --> 00:37:11,005
The Mongols have been
bothering us for a long time.

381
00:37:11,683 --> 00:37:13,923
We've been dealing with them
for a long time.

382
00:37:16,154 --> 00:37:20,154
How will it be from now on? What will
the emperor say when he finds out?

383
00:37:24,913 --> 00:37:27,463
What if something worse
happens to Osman Bey?

384
00:37:36,708 --> 00:37:38,858
If something happens to Osman Bey...

385
00:37:38,950 --> 00:37:43,460
... this Tent and many others
will rise, Princess.

386
00:37:47,712 --> 00:37:49,302
Don't you worry.

387
00:37:50,820 --> 00:37:53,360
Osman Bey saved many Hatuns like you.

388
00:39:55,527 --> 00:39:58,157
What's the reason for
your unexpected visit?

389
00:39:58,157 --> 00:40:00,017
Where's my uncle, Alişar Bey?

390
00:40:00,647 --> 00:40:03,107
As we know, Dündar Bey is dead.

391
00:40:03,672 --> 00:40:08,242
If he's alive, he's not here
as you can see.

392
00:40:09,629 --> 00:40:11,269
Alişar...

393
00:40:11,779 --> 00:40:14,889
Take Dündar out of the hole you
put him in.

394
00:40:14,889 --> 00:40:17,878
Or I'll throw both of you in
bottomless wells.

395
00:40:18,455 --> 00:40:21,495
You're talking to the Banner Lord
Geyhatu assigned.

396
00:40:22,793 --> 00:40:24,643
Watch your words, Balgay!

397
00:40:27,724 --> 00:40:29,344
Or I'll cut your tongue off!

398
00:40:34,076 --> 00:40:38,076
When did you become so brave?

399
00:40:38,491 --> 00:40:39,731
Huh?

400
00:40:57,063 --> 00:41:01,603
As I see, two enemies have
united against me.

401
00:41:06,290 --> 00:41:08,530
I didn't know that I scared you this much.

402
00:41:08,530 --> 00:41:10,260
Cut it short, Alişar!

403
00:41:11,044 --> 00:41:12,564
Where is my uncle?

404
00:41:13,755 --> 00:41:17,055
Everyone is talking about
how you killed your uncle.

405
00:41:18,822 --> 00:41:21,142
He's probably where you buried him!

406
00:41:21,338 --> 00:41:22,698
Alişar...

407
00:41:26,315 --> 00:41:30,315
You're wrong if you think you're the boss
just because you have someone's word.

408
00:41:30,570 --> 00:41:33,030
I don't care about your Bannerlordship!

409
00:41:34,435 --> 00:41:38,435
I'll ask one last time.
Where is Dündar Bey?

410
00:41:39,867 --> 00:41:42,677
He's probably where you buried him!

411
00:41:45,155 --> 00:41:51,525
Balgay. Are you lying?
Or is he lying?

412
00:42:01,479 --> 00:42:02,499
Kongar!

413
00:42:03,686 --> 00:42:05,356
Search the palace.

414
00:42:25,630 --> 00:42:27,580
What is it, Alişar?

415
00:42:28,159 --> 00:42:30,369
You've become dense like a bow.

416
00:42:31,177 --> 00:42:33,147
What is it that you hide?

417
00:42:40,738 --> 00:42:43,818
I'm not the one who
is supposed to become dense.

418
00:42:44,366 --> 00:42:45,466
It's you.

419
00:42:46,600 --> 00:42:50,330
You're searching the palace of the Banner
Lord assigned by Geyhatu.

420
00:42:50,330 --> 00:42:57,130
Aren't you afraid? On top of that,
with a rebel who killed the Kayı's Bey.

421
00:42:58,370 --> 00:43:00,870
Kayı's Bey is my father.

422
00:43:01,656 --> 00:43:03,486
My brother is his deputy.

423
00:43:04,868 --> 00:43:09,298
The real rebel is my uncle
who you're hiding!

424
00:43:13,101 --> 00:43:15,511
How will you deal with this, Alişar?

425
00:43:18,292 --> 00:43:20,852
I'm the Banner Lord.

426
00:43:20,852 --> 00:43:24,382
The Bey is who I declare.

427
00:43:24,382 --> 00:43:29,502
We choose our Beys with Oghuz tradition.
Not words!

428
00:43:30,680 --> 00:43:33,010
My brother gets his power from this.

429
00:43:34,874 --> 00:43:37,254
Where do you get your power, Alişar?

430
00:43:39,715 --> 00:43:41,535
You killed Batur.

431
00:43:42,671 --> 00:43:44,971
Dündar is lost.

432
00:43:46,208 --> 00:43:48,528
What kind of a tradition is this,
Osman Bey?

433
00:43:48,528 --> 00:43:52,528
We neither killed Batur
nor did we betrayed our uncle.

434
00:43:53,884 --> 00:43:56,454
The roads lead to you, Alişar.

435
00:43:57,501 --> 00:44:00,101
When I bring this trick to the light...

436
00:44:00,793 --> 00:44:03,585
You'll look for a hole to hide in!

437
00:44:05,675 --> 00:44:11,315
Everything that comes to Kayı Tribe is
because of your arrogance, Osman.

438
00:44:11,345 --> 00:44:15,065
You can't teach me!

439
00:44:17,787 --> 00:44:23,337
It's over.
You can't escape now.

440
00:44:39,620 --> 00:44:42,320
There is nobody in the mansion.

441
00:44:59,673 --> 00:45:02,513
Who is fool now, huh?

442
00:45:03,620 --> 00:45:09,130
So, someone is lying.

443
00:45:10,018 --> 00:45:16,188
Eeeh, your alliance is over now.

444
00:45:19,386 --> 00:45:24,566
- Do you know why I don't kill you?
- Why?

445
00:45:24,566 --> 00:45:31,111
Because nobody should see that Osman
Bey kills a Muslim in front of Mongols.

446
00:45:32,121 --> 00:45:39,131
However, the next time we face each other,
I will take your head off your chest.

447
00:45:39,248 --> 00:45:43,938
Then, they will witness a Munafiq's
(factious) death.

448
00:46:13,316 --> 00:46:16,456
Are you trying to fool me with your
little brain?

449
00:46:17,684 --> 00:46:24,214
Don't let me see you again, or
I will crush you.

450
00:46:55,944 --> 00:47:01,488
Your information is not true, Balgay.
You told me that my uncle is with Alişar.

451
00:47:01,488 --> 00:47:09,148
- We both know he is lying.
- A good commander has good spies.

452
00:47:09,734 --> 00:47:16,284
If your spies fool you, that means
the Mongol army's situation is awful.

453
00:47:20,121 --> 00:47:25,161
Still, I will keep my promise.

454
00:47:27,732 --> 00:47:32,192
You wish to learn who has the laws of
Genghiz Khan.

455
00:47:33,191 --> 00:47:35,321
Let me tell you.

456
00:47:37,728 --> 00:47:41,008
I gave them to Yannis.

457
00:47:42,783 --> 00:47:45,963
What are you looking for is in
Kulucahisar Castle.

458
00:47:47,121 --> 00:47:50,877
You are setting me against my fellows.

459
00:47:50,877 --> 00:47:56,937
You say you've had many wars, but you still
can't distinguish between friend and enemy

460
00:48:00,149 --> 00:48:05,829
Yannis wanted Genghis Khan's laws
in return of your life.

461
00:48:12,310 --> 00:48:14,980
Now you can take care of him.

462
00:48:19,288 --> 00:48:26,674
Kongar, get ready. You'll turn
Kulucahisar Castle into a grave.

463
00:48:26,674 --> 00:48:30,034
You need to bring me what belongs
to me.

464
00:48:30,136 --> 00:48:35,016
Or I will take your life.

465
00:48:36,302 --> 00:48:39,252
Yes, Commander Balgay.

466
00:48:40,408 --> 00:48:42,588
Where will you go?

467
00:48:42,981 --> 00:48:48,851
I will confront those who degraded me
in front of Osman Bey.

468
00:49:26,685 --> 00:49:29,565
Osman Bey, they wait for you.

469
00:49:29,982 --> 00:49:32,472
I will arrive.

470
00:49:51,442 --> 00:49:56,942
Mother, why are we returning to the tribe?
Don't you know what is going to happen?

471
00:49:56,998 --> 00:50:02,008
I know, of course, but this is
what your father wants.

472
00:50:03,743 --> 00:50:08,843
You can't escape from what you have done,
my Aygül.

473
00:50:34,551 --> 00:50:38,394
- Father...
- My Bey, are you okay?

474
00:50:38,394 --> 00:50:40,614
I'm fine, I'm fine.

475
00:50:41,225 --> 00:50:47,245
I suffer from both an arrow wound and
ulcer.

476
00:50:47,431 --> 00:50:51,021
But, I am fine now, don't worry.

477
00:50:51,052 --> 00:50:55,262
Dündar Bey, do you want to give a break?

478
00:50:57,262 --> 00:51:03,207
Saltug, son, gather wood, we'll set fire.

479
00:51:03,207 --> 00:51:05,537
We may get cold.

480
00:51:25,068 --> 00:51:31,628
My Bey...
I have something to tell you.

481
00:51:37,556 --> 00:51:41,256
What's now, Hatun?
Tell me.

482
00:51:44,735 --> 00:51:49,195
Hatun, tell me!
What is your problem?

483
00:51:49,903 --> 00:51:54,806
If you are worried about the tribe,
don't.

484
00:51:54,806 --> 00:51:57,946
We are not guilty.

485
00:52:01,085 --> 00:52:06,465
You are not, but...

486
00:52:06,762 --> 00:52:10,262
I am terrified by what I've done, my Bey.

487
00:52:10,871 --> 00:52:20,631
You should know that first.
I regret disobeying you.

488
00:52:20,742 --> 00:52:25,812
Zöhre, don't push me.

489
00:52:26,107 --> 00:52:29,117
Say what you are going to say?

490
00:52:29,174 --> 00:52:34,224
What have you done, ha?

491
00:52:42,573 --> 00:52:45,733
I've gone to Balgay.

492
00:52:51,459 --> 00:52:57,589
Do you hear what you are saying, Hatun?

493
00:52:59,655 --> 00:53:08,015
My Batur went after Osman
and you rejected him...

494
00:53:08,018 --> 00:53:10,818
I had no choice...

495
00:53:13,176 --> 00:53:16,596
- Father, father don't.
- Go away, let go of me!

496
00:53:17,546 --> 00:53:22,546
Tell me!
Tell me what you have done!

497
00:53:23,145 --> 00:53:26,225
While my Batur was going after Osman...

498
00:53:26,994 --> 00:53:30,524
I didn't want him to be slaughtered
by Mongols.

499
00:53:31,141 --> 00:53:36,365
I went to Balgay and offered Osman
in return of Batur.

500
00:53:36,365 --> 00:53:38,557
I didn't want my son to be hurt.

501
00:53:38,557 --> 00:53:41,149
What else do you have?!

502
00:53:41,149 --> 00:53:49,429
Then Balgay strangled me to find out
who informed Geyhatu.

503
00:53:51,379 --> 00:53:56,949
Your real problem, my Bey, is that I said
it was Gündüz Bey.

504
00:54:03,451 --> 00:54:07,741
Father! I beg you, don't!
- Get out of my way, Aygül!

505
00:54:18,423 --> 00:54:23,343
What have you done to me, Zöhre?

506
00:54:23,750 --> 00:54:27,160
What troubles have you caused me?

507
00:54:27,492 --> 00:54:31,572
How can you crush me like this?

508
00:54:32,960 --> 00:54:38,200
Take your hands off!
Don't you touch me!

509
00:54:38,999 --> 00:54:45,549
I was feeding a snake all these years!
Pity!

510
00:54:45,549 --> 00:54:49,173
What a shame!

511
00:54:52,870 --> 00:54:57,840
I have a child more precious than my life.

512
00:54:57,911 --> 00:55:01,511
I'm not killing you for her sake.
But...

513
00:55:01,563 --> 00:55:09,843
... if I see you do one more thing wrong,
I won't listen to her and I'll kill you.

514
00:55:09,850 --> 00:55:12,200
Remember this.

515
00:55:13,003 --> 00:55:17,403
This sword I stuck into the dirt...

516
00:55:17,407 --> 00:55:20,977
... will pierce your heart.

517
00:55:23,085 --> 00:55:27,185
It will be your end.

518
00:55:45,013 --> 00:55:48,383
Isn't it hard living in a Tent,
Bala Hatun?

519
00:55:48,405 --> 00:55:50,975
Don't you get cold in winter?

520
00:55:52,411 --> 00:55:56,021
Don't these tents break down in rain?

521
00:55:58,121 --> 00:56:04,711
They are warm in winter, and cool in
summer. Not one drop of rain can get in.

522
00:56:06,685 --> 00:56:13,195
We call them haircloth tents. Made from
felt. They are durable.

523
00:56:15,875 --> 00:56:19,503
Do servants and Masters live in
different tents?

524
00:56:19,503 --> 00:56:21,623
How do you decide?

525
00:56:22,247 --> 00:56:24,007
Servants?

526
00:56:26,202 --> 00:56:30,706
Princess... We don't have masters.

527
00:56:30,706 --> 00:56:38,111
We are all equal. We don't have
any servants or masters.

528
00:56:38,111 --> 00:56:41,842
How can that be? Who does your footwork?

529
00:56:41,842 --> 00:56:48,712
Everyone does their own work. Our beliefs
don't allow us to have slaves, Princess.

530
00:56:49,863 --> 00:56:52,593
In Islam, we only serve Allah.

531
00:56:53,000 --> 00:56:56,280
Hatuns and men have different duties.

532
00:56:56,610 --> 00:57:00,016
Everyone does what they do the best.

533
00:57:00,016 --> 00:57:02,166
What about your King?

534
00:57:03,273 --> 00:57:06,323
Is Osman Bey your King?

535
00:57:09,689 --> 00:57:12,929
Beys manage our Tent.

536
00:57:13,481 --> 00:57:18,121
Kayı Tent's Bey is Osman Bey's brother
Gündüz Bey.

537
00:57:23,111 --> 00:57:25,721
Everything is different.

538
00:57:25,936 --> 00:57:27,896
Very different.

539
00:57:27,898 --> 00:57:34,058
Thank Jesus Christ he sent Osman Bey
and you for me.

540
00:57:38,202 --> 00:57:40,982
I will pray for all of you.

541
00:58:04,869 --> 00:58:08,775
Go inside the tent. Stay inside, Princess.

542
00:58:08,775 --> 00:58:11,055
What is going on, Bala Hatun?

543
00:58:17,907 --> 00:58:21,677
- What are you going to do?
- Get inside the tent. Relax.

544
00:58:21,685 --> 00:58:24,475
I'll see who's coming.

545
00:58:40,090 --> 00:58:44,670
- Welcome Dündar Bey!
- Welcome, my Bey!

546
00:59:03,143 --> 00:59:05,633
Welcome, Dündar Bey.

547
00:59:08,424 --> 00:59:10,774
Welcome, my Bey.

548
00:59:35,852 --> 00:59:44,902
My Allah! May my Allah don't keep anyone
away from their homeland!

549
00:59:45,454 --> 00:59:53,044
May my Allah, who allowed me to return,
allow me to take my revenge.

550
00:59:55,886 --> 00:59:59,916
Amin, father. Amin.

551
01:00:14,232 --> 01:00:17,732
Welcome, my Bey.

552
01:00:17,983 --> 01:00:20,003
Welcome, my Bey.

553
01:00:25,752 --> 01:00:28,512
Welcome, my Bey.

554
01:00:40,474 --> 01:00:42,784
Uncle!

555
01:00:44,352 --> 01:00:47,272
How can you return to this Tent?

556
01:00:48,952 --> 01:00:55,333
How can you stand before me?

557
01:00:55,333 --> 01:01:01,463
You got up on my throne right after
I died, and you're calling me out.

558
01:01:15,052 --> 01:01:23,042
We know that you're working with Alişar.
Alps saw you with Alişar at Batur's funeral.

559
01:01:24,013 --> 01:01:29,940
Don't you lie no more and
make a fool out of yourself!

560
01:01:29,940 --> 01:01:36,290
Thanks to Alişar Bey, I found
my son's killers.

561
01:01:36,627 --> 01:01:41,020
What did you do? Huh?
What did you do?

562
01:01:41,020 --> 01:01:46,136
You attacked my daughter and my woman!

563
01:01:46,136 --> 01:01:50,776
If you tracked the infidels instead...

564
01:01:50,776 --> 01:01:56,576
... I wouldn't need to work
with Alişar Bey!

565
01:01:58,068 --> 01:02:01,148
What are you talking about, uncle?

566
01:02:02,238 --> 01:02:05,658
Who are Batur's killers?
How did you find out?

567
01:02:05,658 --> 01:02:10,728
Are you asking this question now?

568
01:02:10,938 --> 01:02:16,518
You left me alone with my pain.

569
01:02:16,564 --> 01:02:21,864
With Alişar, we found the Mongol
soldiers who killed my Batur.

570
01:02:21,864 --> 01:02:27,104
I took my son's revenge with these hands.

571
01:02:29,070 --> 01:02:34,580
What did you do? Huh?
What?

572
01:02:36,082 --> 01:02:41,482
Wait, uncle? Breathe.

573
01:02:42,112 --> 01:02:46,282
Let's talk about this calmly.

574
01:02:46,282 --> 01:02:49,072
I'll say what you did.

575
01:02:50,661 --> 01:03:00,691
You sent my daughter and wife to
Alişar Bey's palace for nothing!

576
01:03:01,163 --> 01:03:06,443
It wasn't enough. You tried to kill me.

577
01:03:06,811 --> 01:03:10,710
We're all here.

578
01:03:10,710 --> 01:03:17,340
If it wasn't enough, kill us.

579
01:03:17,824 --> 01:03:23,615
We sent Zöhre Hatun and Aygül to Alişar's
palace for a reason!

580
01:03:23,615 --> 01:03:28,745
I know. I'm aware of everything.

581
01:03:29,396 --> 01:03:34,369
But before we blame someone...

582
01:03:34,369 --> 01:03:40,709
... we listen to them, as it's our
tradition. We don't hurt anyone...

583
01:03:41,136 --> 01:03:44,746
... before listening to their reasons.

584
01:03:47,300 --> 01:03:53,340
Zöhre Hatun did everything to
look for solutions.

585
01:03:53,391 --> 01:03:56,561
Not for throwing our Tent into the fire.

586
01:03:58,226 --> 01:04:04,675
If someone's going to call people out,
it's me.

587
01:04:04,675 --> 01:04:10,385
Of course, there are questions to be
asked, answers to be given.

588
01:04:10,444 --> 01:04:17,134
Everything has a time.

589
01:04:18,363 --> 01:04:27,333
From now on, Dündar Bey will make
everyone pay for what they have done.

590
01:04:28,646 --> 01:04:30,866
Know that.

591
01:04:33,608 --> 01:04:36,128
Know that.

592
01:05:15,083 --> 01:05:17,753
What is it, Melik?

593
01:05:17,870 --> 01:05:20,532
Your eyes are cloudy.

594
01:05:20,532 --> 01:05:23,961
Can we trust Dündar Bey, my Bey?

595
01:05:23,961 --> 01:05:27,071
What if he is playing with us?

596
01:05:32,195 --> 01:05:37,435
When you're feeding a lamb,
you cut its wool.

597
01:05:37,451 --> 01:05:41,457
You wash it and cut again.

598
01:05:41,457 --> 01:05:45,808
First time, the animal gets scared.

599
01:05:45,808 --> 01:05:48,099
Then it gets used to it.

600
01:05:48,099 --> 01:05:54,083
When you're going to kill it, it thinks
that its wool will be cut again.

601
01:05:54,083 --> 01:06:01,453
But the knife is on its neck
this time, not on its wool.

602
01:06:01,867 --> 01:06:03,327
For now, we'll...

603
01:06:04,177 --> 01:06:05,737
... cut Dündar's wool.

604
01:06:09,413 --> 01:06:13,823
So that he doesn't scare when
I put a knife on his throat.

605
01:06:14,777 --> 01:06:22,257
As long as he has such greed and grudge,
he'll always serve us.

606
01:06:29,650 --> 01:06:30,610
Zorba.

607
01:06:31,085 --> 01:06:32,205
Yes, my Bey.

608
01:06:32,796 --> 01:06:34,766
Take this letter to Konya
right now.

609
01:06:35,859 --> 01:06:36,989
Be on the alert.

610
01:06:39,104 --> 01:06:41,664
Protect this letter at the cost of
your life.

611
01:06:41,868 --> 01:06:43,618
The order is order, my bey.

612
01:06:54,917 --> 01:06:56,277
Balgay.

613
01:06:57,522 --> 01:07:01,402
Now, let him know he has
the power.

614
01:07:02,129 --> 01:07:06,129
We'll see what he will do when
Geyhatu learns everything.

615
01:07:06,307 --> 01:07:07,987
What do you think he'll do, my bey?

616
01:07:08,325 --> 01:07:12,105
He'll butter up and apologize to you.

617
01:07:14,572 --> 01:07:18,972
I will make Balgay dance like a dancer boy
in these lands.

618
01:07:41,454 --> 01:07:42,464
Come on!

619
01:07:44,954 --> 01:07:46,114
Come on!

620
01:07:53,195 --> 01:07:55,255
Fortunately, I found you, my bey.

621
01:07:55,738 --> 01:07:58,388
You didn't because I wasn't lost, Boran.

622
01:07:59,744 --> 01:08:02,134
I took the princess to them safely,
bey.

623
01:08:02,349 --> 01:08:03,339
Thank you.

624
01:08:04,963 --> 01:08:06,523
I got some things to do.

625
01:08:07,291 --> 01:08:09,651
Alişar and my uncle do something
behind me.

626
01:08:10,302 --> 01:08:12,692
I will not show up until I solve it.

627
01:08:15,313 --> 01:08:16,813
Inform Bala Hatun.

628
01:08:17,439 --> 01:08:18,769
I'm waiting for her.

629
01:08:19,350 --> 01:08:21,410
She knows where I'll be waiting.

630
01:08:22,812 --> 01:08:27,112
But take some soldiers on Konya road to
lay an ambush.

631
01:08:27,990 --> 01:08:33,230
We need to know what he's talking with Konya
in order to know what Alişar is thinking.

632
01:08:33,412 --> 01:08:34,772
What if we learn?

633
01:08:34,902 --> 01:08:37,362
If you have information, you come.

634
01:08:37,503 --> 01:08:39,733
I'll do your order with great pleasure.

635
01:09:31,447 --> 01:09:33,177
Welcome, Dündar Bey.

636
01:09:33,307 --> 01:09:35,177
We become peaceful thanks to you.

637
01:09:35,267 --> 01:09:36,387
May you live long.

638
01:09:37,205 --> 01:09:40,765
I will never forget your loyalty.

639
01:09:44,307 --> 01:09:48,257
When will we destroy their Tent, my bey?

640
01:09:48,619 --> 01:09:50,529
I came here for one reason.

641
01:09:51,726 --> 01:09:54,216
First, let's solve it.

642
01:09:55,253 --> 01:10:00,173
Then, I will kill all of them.

643
01:10:03,149 --> 01:10:04,219
Alişar Bey.

644
01:10:04,521 --> 01:10:06,371
I have some important news for you.

645
01:10:07,153 --> 01:10:09,473
Osman is working with Balgay.

646
01:10:14,594 --> 01:10:15,884
Understood.

647
01:10:41,422 --> 01:10:45,682
Why this misbeliever is in your
mansion, Alişar Bey?

648
01:10:48,400 --> 01:10:51,590
It is the duty of bannerlord to control
here, Dündar Bey.

649
01:10:52,228 --> 01:10:56,068
Helen, who the princess Sofia sent,
brought some important news.

650
01:10:56,217 --> 01:11:00,777
The princess who has been sent to
marry with Geyhatu has disappeared.

651
01:11:05,610 --> 01:11:09,520
I think Osman is the reason for this.

652
01:11:09,896 --> 01:11:10,976
It didn't finish.

653
01:11:11,331 --> 01:11:13,241
Your nephew is coming here.

654
01:11:13,658 --> 01:11:18,178
With Balgay who he is working with.

655
01:11:20,478 --> 01:11:22,778
Didn't I tell you, Alişar Bey?

656
01:11:24,738 --> 01:11:28,988
I saw a lot of things with these eyes.

657
01:11:29,699 --> 01:11:30,839
I'll wait for them.

658
01:11:31,616 --> 01:11:33,836
But, they shouldn't see you here,
Dündar Bey.

659
01:11:34,821 --> 01:11:39,401
From now on, your duty is Tent.

660
01:11:40,651 --> 01:11:48,691
If the princess is in the Tent, wouldn't taking
her to Geyhatu make you more powerful?

661
01:11:49,743 --> 01:11:54,303
Also, Geyhatu will give whatever we want.

662
01:11:55,128 --> 01:11:57,098
All Mongol golds will be ours.

663
01:11:57,879 --> 01:12:00,809
We'll get rid of Osman and Balgay.

664
01:12:04,171 --> 01:12:09,921
You will be docile in the Tent in order to
save the princess, Dündar Bey.

665
01:12:10,719 --> 01:12:13,879
You will hold your grudge for some time.

666
01:12:14,796 --> 01:12:15,886
What about?

667
01:12:19,318 --> 01:12:26,298
I would eat their raw livers in order to
take my revenge.

668
01:12:26,656 --> 01:12:27,876
Raw liver.

669
01:12:30,793 --> 01:12:34,263
Your first wife and son are on the road,
my bey.

670
01:12:34,517 --> 01:12:35,547
Thank you.

671
01:12:36,639 --> 01:12:40,509
When my braveman comes here, we'll
be more powerful, I hope.

672
01:12:42,434 --> 01:12:43,234
Now...

673
01:12:46,750 --> 01:12:48,390
Listen to me carefully.

674
01:12:50,401 --> 01:12:55,911
There is a Byzantine woman taken
into Tent secretly.

675
01:12:59,644 --> 01:13:00,954
Byzantine woman?

676
01:13:02,746 --> 01:13:04,146
Nobody said us.

677
01:13:04,864 --> 01:13:06,464
They took a precaution.

678
01:13:07,334 --> 01:13:08,514
But you'll find.

679
01:13:08,704 --> 01:13:10,094
What are we gonna do?

680
01:13:10,194 --> 01:13:11,044
Kill her?

681
01:13:11,504 --> 01:13:13,024
We'll kidnap her.

682
01:13:14,241 --> 01:13:17,081
Trace and follow.

683
01:13:24,266 --> 01:13:26,186
Don't feel sorry for her.

684
01:13:26,581 --> 01:13:29,511
But never get caught.

685
01:13:29,655 --> 01:13:30,505
Got it.

686
01:13:32,443 --> 01:13:33,993
Thank you.

687
01:13:34,368 --> 01:13:35,798
Thank you, my bey.

688
01:13:36,433 --> 01:13:37,533
Go.

689
01:13:54,194 --> 01:13:55,314
You sent for me.

690
01:13:55,504 --> 01:13:56,584
What's happening, Helen?

691
01:13:56,674 --> 01:13:57,624
Who is coming?

692
01:14:00,093 --> 01:14:02,023
An important guest of ours.

693
01:14:22,530 --> 01:14:23,410
Here.

694
01:14:24,430 --> 01:14:25,670
He has come.

695
01:14:31,383 --> 01:14:32,873
Commander Kongar.

696
01:14:33,245 --> 01:14:34,225
Welcome.

697
01:14:36,047 --> 01:14:38,657
We would like to be prepared for you.

698
01:14:39,097 --> 01:14:40,567
But there was no time.

699
01:14:40,660 --> 01:14:42,410
Where is Princess Sofia?

700
01:14:43,483 --> 01:14:44,973
Not in castle.

701
01:14:45,879 --> 01:14:48,559
She wanted me to take care of you.

702
01:14:56,455 --> 01:15:01,415
You're either dumb or you trust your God
so much.

703
01:15:07,448 --> 01:15:10,238
If I want, I can destroy this castle.

704
01:15:10,778 --> 01:15:13,968
But there isn't even one soldier of you
on your ramparts.

705
01:15:16,781 --> 01:15:19,001
Do you defend your castle like this?

706
01:15:24,195 --> 01:15:30,175
If we saw you as an enemy, destroying
such an enemy wouldn't even be a pleasure.

707
01:15:34,891 --> 01:15:39,211
My soldiers protect us just from Turks,
commander Kongar.

708
01:15:39,768 --> 01:15:42,988
They can't protect us from such a great
commander.

709
01:15:43,490 --> 01:15:44,270
Shut up!

710
01:15:51,611 --> 01:15:56,911
As you know I was gonna come here, you
know for what I came.

711
01:15:57,491 --> 01:15:58,741
Of course, I know.

712
01:15:59,432 --> 01:16:01,772
But first come in if you like.

713
01:16:02,434 --> 01:16:04,644
I'll prepare a room for you and take
a rest.

714
01:16:07,508 --> 01:16:09,008
Don't mess with me.

715
01:16:13,423 --> 01:16:15,643
Give what belongs to Balgay.

716
01:16:16,852 --> 01:16:21,292
You give it with your own hands so that
my soldiers don't destroy your soldiers...

717
01:16:21,479 --> 01:16:23,609
...with their strong fists.

718
01:16:24,870 --> 01:16:26,430
Don't waste my time.

719
01:16:26,842 --> 01:16:28,652
I don't have any time to wait.

720
01:16:28,772 --> 01:16:29,832
Come on!

721
01:16:44,535 --> 01:16:45,645
Ayaz.

722
01:16:45,981 --> 01:16:50,871
He said whoever go to Konya, stop them.

723
01:16:51,454 --> 01:16:54,114
I hope we won't go back without
doing anything, brother.

724
01:16:54,304 --> 01:16:56,774
Osman is struggling to be
an Alp for a long time.

725
01:16:57,257 --> 01:16:59,587
Do you hear what're you saying,
Dumrul brother.

726
01:17:00,003 --> 01:17:06,463
Many Valiants in Oghuz want to clash
side by side with Osman Bey.

727
01:17:14,090 --> 01:17:15,890
Here, infidels are coming.

728
01:17:18,707 --> 01:17:21,437
Long live with your intelligence,
Osman Bey.

729
01:17:47,729 --> 01:17:50,149
What do you think you are doing, panders?

730
01:17:51,355 --> 01:17:52,445
Get down!

731
01:17:52,601 --> 01:17:53,821
Or I'll kill you.

732
01:17:57,054 --> 01:17:59,304
Or I'll kill you without hesitating.

733
01:18:16,948 --> 01:18:18,448
Salamun Alaikum.

734
01:18:18,997 --> 01:18:20,437
Assalamualaikum.

735
01:18:20,995 --> 01:18:23,925
May Allah bless you with
plentifulness, Osman.

736
01:18:26,186 --> 01:18:27,286
Here you are.

737
01:18:37,672 --> 01:18:42,582
When the princess was kidnapped, Geyhatu
went crazy in his palace.

738
01:18:45,208 --> 01:18:49,218
The Byzantine Ruler who relies on Moghol
went crazy.

739
01:18:50,146 --> 01:18:52,046
We defeated them.

740
01:18:52,479 --> 01:18:53,639
May you live long.

741
01:18:53,709 --> 01:18:54,969
May you live long, too.

742
01:18:56,551 --> 01:19:01,011
Balgay confronted me. He
wanted to kidnap the princess.

743
01:19:02,572 --> 01:19:05,422
He wants to take back his lost
reputation.

744
01:19:06,318 --> 01:19:14,748
Even if we lose everything, we should
protect our soul and reputation always.

745
01:19:15,884 --> 01:19:19,884
Well, how do we lose our reputation?

746
01:19:22,240 --> 01:19:30,750
Human being, in this mortal life, struggles
to death in order to not lose the reputation.

747
01:19:31,185 --> 01:19:41,475
But, being ungratefulness and thanklesness
they lose their reputation towards Allah.

748
01:19:44,167 --> 01:19:51,757
Because our Allah's mercy is greater than
his rage, we survive after all.

749
01:19:52,136 --> 01:20:00,686
But, there isn't anything worse than losing
the reputation of a government, son.

750
01:20:01,915 --> 01:20:06,195
Well. How does a government lose
reputation?

751
01:20:08,655 --> 01:20:13,257
If the morals of the society which make the
government a government get out of order...

752
01:20:14,257 --> 01:20:18,017
...it means the reputation has
started to be lost.

753
01:20:20,180 --> 01:20:24,180
How do we understand that?

754
01:20:25,820 --> 01:20:28,640
If scholars start to lose their
nobility...

755
01:20:29,719 --> 01:20:33,089
If there is injustice...

756
01:20:33,599 --> 01:20:38,559
If there isn't any respect to mother
and father and families break down...

757
01:20:39,232 --> 01:20:41,902
If there isn't any love between couples...

758
01:20:42,190 --> 01:20:48,310
If divorcing is increasing and there
isn't any demand for the knowledge...

759
01:20:48,400 --> 01:20:50,590
If no one cares about intelligence...

760
01:20:51,329 --> 01:20:55,439
If the believers don't live
like they believe...

761
01:20:56,395 --> 01:20:59,925
It means the government is losing
its reputation.

762
01:21:04,183 --> 01:21:08,523
In such a case, what the leader of
society should do?

763
01:21:09,266 --> 01:21:12,456
Leaders are like a reflection
of society.

764
01:21:13,391 --> 01:21:16,431
The society sees them like themselves.

765
01:21:16,689 --> 01:21:19,989
So, the leader himself should be moral.

766
01:21:20,392 --> 01:21:22,922
Everybody should know him as a guide.

767
01:21:23,349 --> 01:21:27,999
They should try to be like him
and live like him.

768
01:21:28,715 --> 01:21:37,125
Our deceased prophet, he turned
stone-hearted people into merciful people.

769
01:21:37,368 --> 01:21:40,878
He took out the water of mercy from
the desert that...

770
01:21:41,032 --> 01:21:43,262
...will help people to solve
their problems.

771
01:21:45,006 --> 01:21:49,006
Now, there's a new duty.

772
01:21:51,619 --> 01:21:55,749
We'll take the road to spoil new
plans.

773
01:21:58,144 --> 01:22:01,534
The expedition is ours and the victory is
Allah's.

774
01:22:02,808 --> 01:22:04,238
I'm listening to you.

775
01:22:16,696 --> 01:22:23,166
Sofia knows that very well
in this chest...

776
01:22:23,806 --> 01:22:26,056
...there is an assurance of heaven
for Balgay.

777
01:22:34,954 --> 01:22:35,804
No!

778
01:22:39,540 --> 01:22:45,690
I hope Balgay won't sell us out to Osman
for the strong sovereign he'll have...

779
01:22:47,194 --> 01:22:50,154
...thanks to those laws.

780
01:22:51,400 --> 01:22:53,470
Commander Kongar.

781
01:23:25,747 --> 01:23:29,477
Also, If I were you...

782
01:23:29,982 --> 01:23:34,632
...I wouldn't trust anything that
Osman has a relationship.

783
01:23:43,046 --> 01:23:45,806
You talk it with Balgay when he comes.

784
01:24:18,543 --> 01:24:20,973
Just for those worthless laws...

785
01:24:22,133 --> 01:24:26,833
The lands that you turn into a bloodbath
will be your end.

786
01:24:32,670 --> 01:24:36,980
Margarit Monastery is planning
something new.

787
01:24:37,242 --> 01:24:38,352
Who are they?

788
01:24:38,464 --> 01:24:43,574
The monks who are determined to
kill all Turks in Bithynia region.

789
01:24:44,870 --> 01:24:48,060
Now, they're planning something new.

790
01:24:48,346 --> 01:24:50,216
By agreeing with Geyhatu...

791
01:24:50,785 --> 01:24:53,545
...they want to ascend someone
else to Byzantium throne.

792
01:24:54,274 --> 01:24:57,244
I need you to find who he is.

793
01:24:58,296 --> 01:25:00,616
We should punish them
heavily.

794
01:25:02,459 --> 01:25:05,509
It won't be that easy to infiltrate
between them.

795
01:25:06,454 --> 01:25:08,444
I need to make preparation.

796
01:25:08,752 --> 01:25:11,192
We'll tell you the necessary information.

797
01:25:13,875 --> 01:25:16,035
The things you've to do is
in this bag.

798
01:25:16,110 --> 01:25:17,040
Examine it

799
01:25:37,488 --> 01:25:41,008
You'll not be alone in this historical
duty.

800
01:25:43,602 --> 01:25:45,372
Who will be my fellow?

801
01:25:54,839 --> 01:26:00,689
A kayı son like you will
be with you.

802
01:26:01,971 --> 01:26:03,761
He'll find you.

803
01:26:04,338 --> 01:26:05,278
Come on.

804
01:26:05,376 --> 01:26:06,376
Good luck.

805
01:26:27,032 --> 01:26:28,262
My Allah...

806
01:26:29,062 --> 01:26:37,062
Please speed this fearless braveman who
takes part in this difficult duty.

807
01:26:38,062 --> 01:26:43,842
His name may be a great mountain
that brutal ones can't conquer.

808
01:26:47,146 --> 01:26:53,906
His sword may cut the infidel cities
like a silk fabric.

809
01:26:54,349 --> 01:26:59,209
But his sword may also be a soul for those
brave men who don't fear from death...

810
01:26:59,405 --> 01:27:00,835
...and open a period.

811
01:27:01,753 --> 01:27:02,603
Amin.

812
01:27:27,744 --> 01:27:30,284
I miss having a conversation with
you, my sister.

813
01:27:30,349 --> 01:27:32,739
Thanks to who make us come together.

814
01:27:44,448 --> 01:27:45,728
Since you've gone...

815
01:27:45,952 --> 01:27:47,582
...Tent is like it's theirs.

816
01:27:49,252 --> 01:27:50,982
We're like foreign among them.

817
01:27:51,687 --> 01:27:53,707
They found the opportunity to do it.

818
01:28:04,516 --> 01:28:06,316
Let it boil.

819
01:28:09,936 --> 01:28:13,496
- Bala Hatun spends a lot of time here.
- Yes.

820
01:28:14,125 --> 01:28:17,225
She's so afraid that she may remain
separate from Osman.

821
01:28:17,990 --> 01:28:20,700
She's always with Selcan Hatun.

822
01:28:24,979 --> 01:28:28,719
- Great job, Hatun. It's beautiful.
- Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

823
01:28:33,742 --> 01:28:35,482
It will tinge its color.

824
01:28:53,084 --> 01:28:54,644
They never stop.

825
01:28:54,881 --> 01:28:57,001
They're full of mischief.

826
01:29:00,332 --> 01:29:02,212
Welcome, Zöhre Hatun.

827
01:29:12,942 --> 01:29:14,732
Zöhre Hatun...

828
01:29:15,351 --> 01:29:18,381
Please don't leave us to
their hands again.

829
01:29:19,091 --> 01:29:21,161
They think they're the owner of the tent.

830
01:29:21,197 --> 01:29:23,967
They're being obstinate.

831
01:29:26,152 --> 01:29:28,792
They brought a new girl to the tent.

832
01:29:30,012 --> 01:29:30,992
Girl?

833
01:29:31,842 --> 01:29:35,612
- Who? Why did she come?
- I don't know.

834
01:29:35,975 --> 01:29:37,725
They protect her.

835
01:29:40,973 --> 01:29:43,573
Bala and Selcan Hatun take care of her.

836
01:29:46,931 --> 01:29:49,301
We'll see about it.

837
01:29:52,632 --> 01:29:55,702
We'll bend their necks.

838
01:29:57,773 --> 01:30:00,013
Look at Bala Hatun.

839
01:30:00,429 --> 01:30:04,429
She thinks she's the wife of
Osman. Look at her.

840
01:30:04,983 --> 01:30:07,453
She's so big-headed.

841
01:30:09,345 --> 01:30:12,175
We'll take care of them.

842
01:30:13,228 --> 01:30:16,228
But I need your help.

843
01:30:17,174 --> 01:30:21,414
- We shouldn't do anything that will turn heads to us.
- We should.

844
01:30:22,581 --> 01:30:25,901
But not to us.

845
01:30:28,236 --> 01:30:30,916
We'll burn those.

846
01:30:34,198 --> 01:30:35,448
Now...

847
01:30:37,395 --> 01:30:40,435
We'll take care of their guest.

848
01:30:40,716 --> 01:30:44,276
So that the girl is taken care
of Selcan Hatun and Bala...

849
01:30:44,863 --> 01:30:49,503
then they should lose her.

850
01:30:50,628 --> 01:30:54,628
If the girl is important for
them, it is for Osman too.

851
01:30:58,208 --> 01:31:01,018
Aygül, don't worry daughter.

852
01:31:01,394 --> 01:31:05,814
I won't do anything without
your father's consent.

853
01:31:10,563 --> 01:31:12,123
Come on.

854
01:31:37,438 --> 01:31:41,538
Allah knows what you're talking about.

855
01:31:41,792 --> 01:31:44,902
You have your eyes on me
all the time, Selcan Hatun.

856
01:31:46,481 --> 01:31:48,171
You look with an evil eye.

857
01:31:51,909 --> 01:31:55,579
Do you refrain from me?

858
01:31:55,913 --> 01:31:59,913
But that's enough. Deal
with your own business.

859
01:32:01,693 --> 01:32:06,493
I keep an eye on the betrayers.

860
01:32:06,660 --> 01:32:08,380
You know.

861
01:32:13,448 --> 01:32:16,298
Don't affect these girls.

862
01:32:17,999 --> 01:32:19,679
I have my eyes on you.

863
01:32:20,163 --> 01:32:24,453
Don't do anything foolish from now on.

864
01:32:25,904 --> 01:32:27,244
Stop.

865
01:32:31,615 --> 01:32:35,025
Don't say anything.

866
01:32:35,184 --> 01:32:38,524
I won't forgive you if I
see your mistake again.

867
01:32:46,593 --> 01:32:48,973
They're doing this all the time.

868
01:32:50,447 --> 01:32:52,947
If we stop, they'll keep doing it.

869
01:32:53,258 --> 01:32:55,438
We should do what's necessary.

870
01:32:55,702 --> 01:32:58,892
They shouldn't harm us anymore.

871
01:33:02,978 --> 01:33:06,718
Tell us. What do you have in your mind?

872
01:33:10,923 --> 01:33:15,233
Burçin will take care of this job.

873
01:33:31,180 --> 01:33:33,400
My Karayel.

874
01:33:34,723 --> 01:33:37,283
We survived many hardships with you.

875
01:33:39,057 --> 01:33:43,057
Many enemies bend their knees.

876
01:33:47,043 --> 01:33:51,313
They're so angry now.

877
01:33:53,030 --> 01:33:56,910
They're waiting for us to fall so
that they will try to kill us.

878
01:33:57,940 --> 01:34:01,940
That's why we have to be
alive all the time.

879
01:34:02,336 --> 01:34:05,536
And awake.

880
01:34:05,675 --> 01:34:09,775
My Karayel. My loyal comrade.

881
01:34:12,424 --> 01:34:13,864
Karayel.

882
01:34:14,968 --> 01:34:19,398
It's time to marry, I guess.

883
01:34:19,959 --> 01:34:23,739
Sheikh Edebalı was on retiring.

884
01:34:24,106 --> 01:34:29,346
I'm saying that, I
should ask for Bala Hatun.

885
01:34:31,288 --> 01:34:33,388
What do you think?

886
01:34:35,680 --> 01:34:37,490
Mashaallah.

887
01:34:39,013 --> 01:34:41,563
What if he doesn't give
her to me, Karayel?

888
01:34:44,505 --> 01:34:48,235
Then I swear I'll abduct Bala.

889
01:34:48,516 --> 01:34:49,836
Huh?

890
01:34:53,441 --> 01:34:57,151
What if...

891
01:34:59,170 --> 01:35:01,370
Bala doesn't want to marry me?

892
01:35:19,902 --> 01:35:22,292
Mashaallah.

893
01:35:22,715 --> 01:35:24,265
My dearest is coming!

894
01:35:50,330 --> 01:35:53,800
- Good riddance, Osman Bey.
- It is.

895
01:35:54,707 --> 01:35:56,297
It is.

896
01:36:12,570 --> 01:36:14,230
It's hyacinth, sir.

897
01:36:14,997 --> 01:36:16,997
It charms the brave.

898
01:36:23,338 --> 01:36:27,338
It's light. I want something more intense.

899
01:36:28,931 --> 01:36:29,871
Of course, my Bey.

900
01:36:37,113 --> 01:36:40,943
White musk. It comes from Arabic lands.

901
01:36:54,400 --> 01:36:57,080
- You're doing your job well.
- Thanks, my Bey.

902
01:37:00,848 --> 01:37:03,268
Always be in my palace.

903
01:37:03,999 --> 01:37:05,619
Your command, my Bey.

904
01:37:11,026 --> 01:37:11,926
My Bey.

905
01:37:13,402 --> 01:37:14,992
Zorba.

906
01:37:16,355 --> 01:37:18,235
What happened to Zorba?

907
01:37:21,447 --> 01:37:24,817
Have you lost your tongue? Talk!

908
01:37:32,130 --> 01:37:33,050
Talk!

909
01:37:35,499 --> 01:37:39,159
Soldiers in the frontier area...
They found Zorba's horse.

910
01:37:39,583 --> 01:37:41,893
They killed the carrier.

911
01:37:42,471 --> 01:37:45,341
Zorba... He's not around.

912
01:37:49,592 --> 01:37:54,072
Do you know what happens
if Zorba is caught by Osman? Huh?!

913
01:37:54,838 --> 01:37:58,258
All of our work will be spoiled.

914
01:37:58,377 --> 01:38:02,437
Osman or Balgay abducted Zorba!

915
01:38:15,685 --> 01:38:18,165
Balgay is after Genghis Khans's laws.

916
01:38:19,574 --> 01:38:22,134
Osman did it.

917
01:38:25,317 --> 01:38:27,287
Inform Dündar Bey immediately.

918
01:38:27,532 --> 01:38:30,282
If Zorba is brought to the tent...

919
01:38:30,344 --> 01:38:32,894
he show no mercy.

920
01:38:33,386 --> 01:38:35,106
He should kill him.

921
01:38:35,608 --> 01:38:38,908
A single mistake will devastate all of us.

922
01:38:39,401 --> 01:38:41,461
Come on. Come on!

923
01:38:42,179 --> 01:38:43,439
Your command, my Bey.

924
01:38:55,046 --> 01:38:57,966
It's good to see you smiling.

925
01:38:58,977 --> 01:39:01,287
Why are you that happy?

926
01:39:01,889 --> 01:39:04,169
My steps are going well.

927
01:39:04,240 --> 01:39:08,400
Everything I do is going well, my Bala.

928
01:39:08,460 --> 01:39:11,240
Why wouldn't I smile?

929
01:39:13,407 --> 01:39:16,307
It's good for you to save the princess.

930
01:39:16,702 --> 01:39:20,702
She's liked our tent. She may
not want to go.

931
01:39:22,920 --> 01:39:25,750
If she wants to stay, our doors are open.

932
01:39:25,780 --> 01:39:30,510
We have our tent, place
and bread to share.

933
01:39:38,329 --> 01:39:40,829
She's the niece of the
Imperial of Byzantine.

934
01:39:45,069 --> 01:39:47,749
She has a big power behind her.

935
01:39:50,016 --> 01:39:53,146
But you know better than me.

936
01:39:54,430 --> 01:39:58,430
I know many things about her. I
inquired about her.

937
01:40:00,932 --> 01:40:04,932
Princess Adelfa is so important, Bala.

938
01:40:05,258 --> 01:40:06,418
So important.

939
01:40:08,512 --> 01:40:12,902
If she's so important, don't
worry Osman Bey.

940
01:40:13,419 --> 01:40:17,939
I'll protect her at the cost of my life.

941
01:40:27,440 --> 01:40:29,680
Princess is important.

942
01:40:30,060 --> 01:40:31,400
But...

943
01:40:31,942 --> 01:40:38,212
if she didn't exist, how could I know
about my woman's concern?

944
01:40:38,953 --> 01:40:41,943
How could I know about your...

945
01:40:41,953 --> 01:40:44,803
love's pettishness?

946
01:41:04,901 --> 01:41:06,011
Bala...

947
01:41:07,936 --> 01:41:11,936
Don't you know that I'll ruin this whole world...

948
01:41:12,660 --> 01:41:16,660
for your tears?

949
01:41:16,825 --> 01:41:19,665
Huh? Don't you know, my Bala?

950
01:41:23,750 --> 01:41:27,480
Why do you upset yourself?

951
01:41:36,472 --> 01:41:38,442
Don't.

952
01:41:43,661 --> 01:41:46,461
Your place in my heart is
getting bigger every day.

953
01:41:47,086 --> 01:41:49,716
The fire of your love burns me every day.

954
01:41:54,238 --> 01:41:56,128
I couldn't...

955
01:41:57,583 --> 01:42:00,423
When love is in the heart...

956
01:42:00,618 --> 01:42:02,408
I lose my mind, Osman.

957
01:42:02,570 --> 01:42:06,850
As long as you love me, I'll never let
anyone harm you.

958
01:42:07,920 --> 01:42:10,030
I'll never let anyone harm you...

959
01:42:11,398 --> 01:42:14,498
Don't worry.

960
01:42:15,122 --> 01:42:17,892
You're destined to me, my Bala.

961
01:42:18,476 --> 01:42:21,746
I'm so thankful to Allah for it.

962
01:42:36,712 --> 01:42:37,702
Osman.

963
01:42:42,395 --> 01:42:44,975
Dündar Bey came to the tent.

964
01:42:45,925 --> 01:42:49,725
Once Alişar Bey took Zöhre
and Aygül to his palace.

965
01:42:50,644 --> 01:42:53,034
Now they're all back.

966
01:42:54,261 --> 01:42:57,771
Dündar Bey said that he found
Batur's killer.

967
01:42:59,462 --> 01:43:02,562
He's said that he'll obey
Gündüz, if necessary.

968
01:43:05,969 --> 01:43:08,769
Alişar and Dündar...
What are they up to again?

969
01:43:25,373 --> 01:43:27,223
Can I come, my Bey?

970
01:43:27,730 --> 01:43:29,220
Come, Boran.

971
01:43:41,992 --> 01:43:43,972
I have important news, my Bey.

972
01:43:58,354 --> 01:43:59,404
My Bey.

973
01:44:02,074 --> 01:44:03,304
What, Saltuk?

974
01:44:03,464 --> 01:44:05,254
I have some news from Alişar Bey.

975
01:44:05,825 --> 01:44:08,405
He thinks that Zorba is abducted
by Osman.

976
01:44:08,473 --> 01:44:10,963
He's told us to trace
Zorba and kill him...

977
01:44:10,963 --> 01:44:13,813
or else, all our plans are ruined.

978
01:44:16,725 --> 01:44:20,905
Oh my Allah. Now we
have to deal with this.

979
01:44:22,448 --> 01:44:24,438
Osman isn't around.

980
01:44:24,503 --> 01:44:28,503
If they have caught Zorba, they
will question him.

981
01:44:31,166 --> 01:44:34,066
Follow one of Osman's Alps.

982
01:44:34,517 --> 01:44:36,227
Trace him.

983
01:44:39,436 --> 01:44:42,506
- If you find...
- Kill him?

984
01:44:43,537 --> 01:44:44,407
Come on.

985
01:45:03,352 --> 01:45:07,042
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

986
01:45:42,435 --> 01:45:45,105
Do you know what ant means, my Akça?

987
01:45:46,071 --> 01:45:48,871
I don't know, my Sheikh.

988
01:45:53,759 --> 01:45:58,149
It's not just an ant if you
know how to look.

989
01:46:01,463 --> 01:46:07,503
It's the verse of the Book of Nature
(Quran) if you know how to read.

990
01:46:11,624 --> 01:46:14,324
It's the sign of
hard work, perseverance and...

991
01:46:14,324 --> 01:46:17,394
collaboration.

992
01:46:21,374 --> 01:46:24,354
Ants are weak when they're alone.

993
01:46:25,106 --> 01:46:26,376
However...

994
01:46:28,304 --> 01:46:35,004
they show how powerful they
are when they're together.

995
01:46:38,441 --> 01:46:40,601
How can we see, my Sheikh?

996
01:46:41,247 --> 01:46:43,297
What should we do to see?

997
01:46:47,875 --> 01:46:53,945
You should see water drops
as a guide, Zulfiqar.

998
01:46:56,338 --> 01:46:59,978
As a water drop, you're alone.

999
01:47:01,751 --> 01:47:06,991
You only vaporize and you disappear.

1000
01:47:09,892 --> 01:47:11,132
But...

1001
01:47:13,038 --> 01:47:17,038
If you go somewhere else...

1002
01:47:18,198 --> 01:47:20,668
you'll be home to the fishes...

1003
01:47:23,096 --> 01:47:28,116
and you'll be water for the dry fields.

1004
01:47:32,918 --> 01:47:37,918
You learn that union is strength.

1005
01:47:40,979 --> 01:47:46,179
Your inability will be your power.

1006
01:47:47,077 --> 01:47:51,077
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

1007
01:47:55,736 --> 01:47:59,736
Allah gives us a mystery in

1008
01:47:59,858 --> 01:48:04,358
Neml Surah (ant Surah).

1009
01:48:06,473 --> 01:48:10,473
Prophet Sulaiman goes on a voyage...

1010
01:48:12,460 --> 01:48:16,010
with his army.

1011
01:48:16,939 --> 01:48:22,849
The army respects the ant law and stop.

1012
01:48:24,701 --> 01:48:26,071
Why?

1013
01:48:30,090 --> 01:48:35,960
Because what makes Prophet
Sulaiman's state big is...

1014
01:48:37,391 --> 01:48:39,961
not that he rules the world.

1015
01:48:43,317 --> 01:48:49,357
It's because even when he rules
the world, he sees the ant law.

1016
01:48:50,539 --> 01:48:53,889
How can we see that law?

1017
01:48:54,989 --> 01:48:57,489
Prophet Sulaiman...

1018
01:48:57,932 --> 01:49:00,932
was the biggest sultan in the world.

1019
01:49:03,632 --> 01:49:08,372
He owned a big land.

1020
01:49:09,615 --> 01:49:13,615
Muslims couldn't find the poor
to help them.

1021
01:49:15,235 --> 01:49:19,235
They were very skillful when
using weapons.

1022
01:49:21,555 --> 01:49:24,905
His army scared cruel ones...

1023
01:49:24,905 --> 01:49:28,905
and became a hope to everyone.

1024
01:49:29,768 --> 01:49:33,768
To learn about this improvement...

1025
01:49:33,768 --> 01:49:39,788
many rulers visited Prophet Sulaiman.

1026
01:49:40,305 --> 01:49:43,635
Belkıs was one of them.

1027
01:49:44,351 --> 01:49:50,231
Visitors were surprised by what they saw.

1028
01:49:52,850 --> 01:49:56,710
Because the moral improvement...

1029
01:49:56,710 --> 01:49:59,040
was prominent.

1030
01:50:01,331 --> 01:50:04,391
People's love of the afterlife...

1031
01:50:04,536 --> 01:50:08,536
...were a lot greater than their love
of life.

1032
01:50:10,364 --> 01:50:13,084
When the time of prayer called...

1033
01:50:14,336 --> 01:50:18,336
...people would run to pray...

1034
01:50:19,074 --> 01:50:23,324
...instead of eating. So they could
thank the one who gave it to them.

1035
01:50:25,555 --> 01:50:29,805
May Allah grant the awakening from
the sleep of blindness...

1036
01:50:30,145 --> 01:50:34,145
...to the ummah of Muhammad.

1037
01:50:35,904 --> 01:50:37,754
-Amin, my Sheikh.
-Inshallah.

1038
01:50:39,383 --> 01:50:42,213
Will we be able to live up to see these
days, my Sheikh?

1039
01:50:42,237 --> 01:50:44,537
Will we be freed from this press?

1040
01:50:46,792 --> 01:50:49,702
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

1041
01:50:53,755 --> 01:50:57,115
Muslims left the compass of science...

1042
01:50:57,759 --> 01:50:59,909
...morals are corrupted...

1043
01:51:00,594 --> 01:51:04,094
...the values that defined us
had been destroyed.

1044
01:51:04,740 --> 01:51:07,090
With the guidance of oracles...

1045
01:51:07,421 --> 01:51:12,741
...if we can be a Suleiman, Zulkarneyn,
Joseph and David of our time...

1046
01:51:12,895 --> 01:51:16,155
...why not, Akça?

1047
01:51:17,634 --> 01:51:23,284
Our good Allah didn't tell us these
parables just as stories...

1048
01:51:24,042 --> 01:51:28,042
...but for us to take them as our
cause...

1049
01:51:29,065 --> 01:51:36,695
...and take the mentioned people
us our guide.

1050
01:51:39,938 --> 01:51:43,938
If we hold Allah's bond strongly...

1051
01:51:45,858 --> 01:51:49,858
...for sure, Allah is the one who
keeps promises.

1052
01:51:55,586 --> 01:51:58,696
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

1053
01:52:08,584 --> 01:52:12,294
My Bey, we hunted Alişar's runner
on his way to Konya.

1054
01:52:12,297 --> 01:52:14,327
And we found this on him.

1055
01:52:18,452 --> 01:52:20,082
Thank you, Boran.

1056
01:52:42,772 --> 01:52:44,922
What does it say, Osman Bey?

1057
01:52:44,976 --> 01:52:48,976
Alişar tells Geyhatu that the princess
is seized by us...

1058
01:52:50,952 --> 01:52:53,592
...invited him here, with his army.

1059
01:52:53,826 --> 01:52:58,456
He says, I'm responsible for the unrest
and Balgay is responsible for helping me.

1060
01:52:58,921 --> 01:53:02,921
And that we are rebels on revolt.

1061
01:53:06,025 --> 01:53:10,565
Now I understand why my uncle came
to the tents out of the blue.

1062
01:53:10,702 --> 01:53:12,712
He will kidnap the princess.

1063
01:53:12,816 --> 01:53:16,366
-What will we do?
-I have an important job.

1064
01:53:16,442 --> 01:53:18,572
Now listen to me carefully.

1065
01:53:18,572 --> 01:53:21,862
You'll stop Dündar Bey from
abducting the princess.

1066
01:53:23,571 --> 01:53:27,571
We should lead my uncle to a trap.
Interrogate Alişar's man.

1067
01:53:27,598 --> 01:53:30,198
Do it away from the tents,
if possible.

1068
01:53:30,281 --> 01:53:34,281
Alişar will do anything he can to take
his man back.

1069
01:53:34,362 --> 01:53:37,232
And you'll breath down on their necks.

1070
01:53:37,279 --> 01:53:38,459
Is it clear?

1071
01:53:39,466 --> 01:53:40,886
Yes, my Bey.

1072
01:53:46,329 --> 01:53:47,449
Yes, my Bey.

1073
01:54:01,770 --> 01:54:05,770
This arrival of Dündar...
...it doesn't seem good.

1074
01:54:08,446 --> 01:54:12,446
Only Allah knows whether it's good
or bad.

1075
01:54:15,389 --> 01:54:18,439
What was I supposed to do,
Bamsı Bey? Huh?

1076
01:54:18,665 --> 01:54:22,245
Was I supposed to send my uncle to
Alişar's mansion?

1077
01:54:25,256 --> 01:54:27,496
Thank you, son. Thank you.

1078
01:54:28,108 --> 01:54:32,108
But when the thief is inside,
a lock is useless.

1079
01:54:48,071 --> 01:54:52,071
We got Zorba, my Bey.
He waits outside the tents.

1080
01:54:54,333 --> 01:54:58,333
Let's go and find his tongue,
Bamsı Bey.

1081
01:54:59,073 --> 01:55:02,193
Let's see what is he hiding.

1082
01:55:03,877 --> 01:55:05,517
Yes, let us do that.

1083
01:55:18,711 --> 01:55:22,071
What's up my nephew?
What's this hurry?

1084
01:55:22,321 --> 01:55:24,341
Where are you going?

1085
01:55:31,359 --> 01:55:35,709
The goods that will go to Yenipazar
are lacking. A caravan is coming.

1086
01:55:35,858 --> 01:55:38,078
I'm going to check them, uncle.

1087
01:55:41,132 --> 01:55:43,842
Thank you, thank you.

1088
01:55:45,336 --> 01:55:48,216
Yenipazar is important for us.

1089
01:55:48,908 --> 01:55:53,558
The goods that will be sold in there
are important for our tents.

1090
01:55:54,547 --> 01:55:58,607
I always say it, when there is no coin...

1091
01:55:59,784 --> 01:56:01,914
...there is no ruling.

1092
01:56:04,381 --> 01:56:08,241
You understand it the best in these tents.

1093
01:56:10,161 --> 01:56:14,161
When you sit on the Bey's throne,
we'll see it closely.

1094
01:56:33,681 --> 01:56:37,911
And another thing I see is your support
for me...

1095
01:56:39,023 --> 01:56:42,763
...despite resentments and ailments,
I can't forget that, my nephew.

1096
01:56:43,856 --> 01:56:48,296
Law stands with power but walks
with experience.

1097
01:56:49,218 --> 01:56:51,778
I see that you are very diligent...

1098
01:56:52,168 --> 01:56:57,008
If there is a task that your uncle can do,
say it freely.

1099
01:57:00,147 --> 01:57:05,467
And my brother, too, would want to see
us like this; shoulder to shoulder.

1100
01:57:26,623 --> 01:57:29,743
Dündar Bey separated the white from
the black.

1101
01:57:29,755 --> 01:57:33,755
Now we should blend both the white
and the black to the red of blood.

1102
01:58:35,773 --> 01:58:37,013
Welcome.

1103
01:58:37,141 --> 01:58:41,141
When I heard that we have a guest,
I wanted to bring a sherbet and a welcome.

1104
01:58:42,436 --> 01:58:45,506
This is our indigenous sherbet.

1105
01:58:50,935 --> 01:58:53,245
We treat it to every newcomer.

1106
01:59:07,755 --> 01:59:11,315
What a lovely smell. What is that
made of?

1107
01:59:11,458 --> 01:59:13,138
We call it cranberry.

1108
01:59:13,917 --> 01:59:17,337
Drink it, sister. Let's see if you'll
like it.

1109
02:00:44,821 --> 02:00:49,551
Don't even try, Zorba.
You can't go anywhere before speaking.

1110
02:00:50,442 --> 02:00:54,442
Do you know what you are doing?
I'm the helper of the bannerlord!

1111
02:00:54,467 --> 02:00:57,127
Alişar Bey will turn this place into
a bloodbath!

1112
02:00:57,227 --> 02:00:57,997
Enough!

1113
02:00:59,575 --> 02:01:03,285
You should think of my Osman Bey's fury!

1114
02:01:06,816 --> 02:01:09,916
You'll soon see what fury is.

1115
02:01:14,292 --> 02:01:16,842
Lower that thing, Saltuğ.

1116
02:01:20,219 --> 02:01:21,379
C'mon.

1117
02:01:32,902 --> 02:01:35,792
The hunter became the hunted.

1118
02:01:41,547 --> 02:01:47,427
Cut a long story short, there is no need
for pointless bickering, my nephew.

1119
02:01:50,022 --> 02:01:54,022
It seems, one calamity is a better teacher
than a thousand counsel.

1120
02:01:56,123 --> 02:02:01,073
I thought about it. What happened
caused me a son.

1121
02:02:05,717 --> 02:02:09,717
When we lost Aybars, I couldn't control
Bamsı Bey.

1122
02:02:11,765 --> 02:02:15,765
Now, I understand him better.

1123
02:02:16,739 --> 02:02:20,739
But we farewelled Aybars with farewells...

1124
02:02:21,148 --> 02:02:27,138
...by saying Allahu Akbar. That was
appropriate for the valiant of Kayı.

1125
02:02:29,698 --> 02:02:32,818
But I farewelled my son...

1126
02:02:33,909 --> 02:02:35,339
...my Batur...

1127
02:02:36,824 --> 02:02:38,484
...all alone.

1128
02:02:48,237 --> 02:02:52,237
It's like there is a furnace burning
right in here.

1129
02:02:55,997 --> 02:03:00,777
It's like, even if this river wouldn't be
enough to put the fire off.

1130
02:03:10,339 --> 02:03:14,899
If you think there is a mistake in
my doings...

1131
02:03:15,669 --> 02:03:18,669
...forgive me because of my pain,
my nephew.

1132
02:03:19,190 --> 02:03:23,190
But after all, there can't be two heads...

1133
02:03:24,214 --> 02:03:25,944
...on a single body.

1134
02:03:30,239 --> 02:03:33,669
Our laws choose you as our Bey.

1135
02:03:34,903 --> 02:03:38,353
And we should follow you.

1136
02:04:05,094 --> 02:04:09,094
Not at all, uncle.
Not at all.

1137
02:04:33,751 --> 02:04:35,671
Have you followed me?

1138
02:04:36,070 --> 02:04:38,280
Untie me and I'll tell you.

1139
02:04:54,041 --> 02:04:57,691
Ayaz, calm down, brother.
Calm down!

1140
02:04:58,171 --> 02:05:02,171
-We need them alive.
-Yes. Yes, we do.

1141
02:05:02,847 --> 02:05:07,137
But since both of them are here,
they must've known of each other.

1142
02:05:19,358 --> 02:05:22,808
Thank Allah that you are helper
of my Dündar Bey.

1143
02:05:23,232 --> 02:05:26,322
Otherwise, I would kill you right away.

1144
02:05:26,777 --> 02:05:30,297
He can't come here before getting
Dündar Bey's approval.

1145
02:05:31,731 --> 02:05:35,331
There is something behind this, brother.
I know there is.

1146
02:06:04,026 --> 02:06:05,866
Hang on, warriors!

1147
02:06:06,668 --> 02:06:08,648
Arrows coming this way!

1148
02:06:13,616 --> 02:06:16,856
There are too many trees, we should
go on foot.

1149
02:06:19,600 --> 02:06:22,510
Ayaz, you stay with them.

1150
02:06:57,766 --> 02:06:59,896
Look, I've brought you food.

1151
02:07:10,793 --> 02:07:12,553
Princess?

1152
02:07:48,515 --> 02:07:49,895
Selcan Hatun!

1153
02:07:52,807 --> 02:07:54,897
What's up my girl?
What's wrong?

1154
02:07:55,102 --> 02:07:57,512
Missing. Adefa is missing,
Selcan Hatun.

1155
02:07:57,751 --> 02:08:00,101
Her tent is empty. I couldn't
find her nearby either.

1156
02:08:00,221 --> 02:08:01,851
What are you saying, Bala?

1157
02:08:01,950 --> 02:08:04,350
Osman Bey summoned me. I went
to meet him.

1158
02:08:04,638 --> 02:08:07,968
He told me that Dündar Bey and his
supporters will try to kidnap Adefa.

1159
02:08:08,296 --> 02:08:10,616
He told me to be cautious.

1160
02:08:10,745 --> 02:08:14,275
I went to Adefa as soon as I came back.
But I was too late, Selcan Hatun.

1161
02:08:15,201 --> 02:08:16,831
We are too late.

1162
02:08:19,359 --> 02:08:21,539
Dündar... You did it again.

1163
02:08:23,020 --> 02:08:26,230
Day that your doings will be exposed,
you and your followers...

1164
02:08:26,668 --> 02:08:29,648
...you will all come to an end.

1165
02:08:31,859 --> 02:08:34,449
Kongar, you'll stay here.

1166
02:08:34,833 --> 02:08:39,253
Do you think that it is too much for me
to carry the laws of Genghis Khan?

1167
02:08:39,714 --> 02:08:43,324
I'll give another task, at least as
honorable as that one.

1168
02:08:43,659 --> 02:08:44,959
What is it?

1169
02:08:53,802 --> 02:08:56,482
You will watch Osman closely.

1170
02:08:56,589 --> 02:09:00,589
A friend of us who is an enemy in truth.

1171
02:09:01,256 --> 02:09:03,516
You'll watch his every step.

1172
02:09:04,229 --> 02:09:07,589
Not only the spirits on the ground
and the sky...

1173
02:09:08,325 --> 02:09:11,365
...there are some others who protect him.

1174
02:09:11,737 --> 02:09:13,987
We need to find the track of this
power.

1175
02:09:14,576 --> 02:09:16,626
Yes, Commander Balgay.

1176
02:09:16,779 --> 02:09:20,779
When I return, Osman will
either obey us...

1177
02:09:21,520 --> 02:09:23,590
...or to his death.

1178
02:10:09,896 --> 02:10:13,086
You won't be alone in this
historical task...

1179
02:10:13,507 --> 02:10:17,507
...a son of Kayı who carries the same
blood with you...

1180
02:10:17,546 --> 02:10:19,426
...will be with you.

1181
02:10:19,580 --> 02:10:21,420
He'll find you.

1182
02:10:21,793 --> 02:11:05,683
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com